cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work package in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "HBM-Meta-Agent: Human Biomonitoring Meta-Analysis Agent"
abstract: >-
  An agent work package for meta-analyses of human internal-exposure biomarker
  concentrations (urine, blood, cord blood, and other matrices). It orchestrates
  the full pipeline from search-strategy construction through screening, quality
  assessment, AI-assisted data extraction with mandatory human proofing, unit and
  statistic standardization (including Wan et al. 2014 formulas S1-S7 and ICRP 89
  urine-correction reference values), sample-size-weighted geometric-mean pooling,
  estimated daily intake, sensitivity analysis, and a closed-loop reviewer-revision
  engine. Ships with a frozen data contract, six human quality gates, reproducible
  Python scripts with self-tests, and six independently triggerable sub-skills.
  Analyte-, matrix-, population- and region-agnostic.
